  "item": "X8",
  "capturedAt": "2026-11-11",
  "question": "X8 phone, round F: does a pin count for a group on a phone, as on desktop it does not (CAP-X8PIN.json, CAP-X8PIN2.json)? CAP-X8PIN2's three Shapes apart (z 1, 3, 2; on the phone stacked in DOM order), the right one pinned with Pin: A, pinned on desktop, then the phone view; B, pinned in the phone view, then read on the phone and back on desktop. Read: one block alone (pin elsewhere), the two groups (pin outside, pin inside) and the pinned block alone, the bar's buttons. Each built twice (A1, A2; B1, B2), Exit Without Saving between, Gestures Probe, nothing saved; the view goes back to Desktop before each exit. Predictions pushed first, ours as built.",
  "rule": "Ours as built: a pin belongs to its layout (layout[bp].sticky). In that layout one block's bar shows Move Forward and Backward when any block in the section is pinned; a group's bar shows them only when a member overlaps a block outside the group, pin or not; on a phone the group bar has no Duplicate and one block's bar has Move Up and Down (editor.js zInfo, groupZ; toolbar.js toolbarItems).",
  "from": "Ours on main, replayed by scripts/lib/x8-phone-pin.mjs: the read's buttons that are present, joined, ' off' on a disabled one.",
